:: Sister Office Brian [micro_event event nobr] {"position":"2675,2900","size":"100,100"}
/* Inline micro event in the Stage 1 main room (micro event 29, "Her rounds" in Define Events): she keeps $brian
   company while he solders. He never looks at her, and he talks more than he has all week. */
<<Media "images/characters/sister/events/office/brian.mp4" 400>>
<p>$brian.name's corner of the office is a nest of cables, anti-static bags and a mug of hot chocolate that has gone cold without anybody touching it. $sister.callName has pulled a chair up next to his, chin in her hand, and she's watching him work like it's a cooking show.</p>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
	{ who: $sister, text: "Okay, and what does that one do?" },
	{ who: $brian, text: "It's a, uh. Voltage regulator. It regulates. Voltage." },
	{ who: $sister, text: "Wow. Does exactly what it says on the box." },
	{ who: $brian, text: "Most things do. If you, uh, name them properly." },
	{ text: "He hasn't looked at her once. He's explaining the board to the board. But his ears have gone bright red, and he's said more in the last five minutes than in the whole meeting this morning." },
	{ who: $sister, text: "Can I try? The little iron thing?" },
	{ who: $brian, text: "No. Uh. I mean, no, it's three hundred and fifty degrees. Sorry. No. You can hold the, uh, the tweezers." },
	{ text: "She holds the tweezers with enormous seriousness, as if he'd handed her a scalpel." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<p>She stays for another twenty minutes. When she finally gets up, $brian.name says 'bye' to the voltage regulator. After she's gone, he pushes his glasses up, looks at the empty chair for a moment and turns it a little, so it faces his desk again.</p>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Morale" 1>>
